+3. Use one modeled workpiece and one **Wire Contour**. For a die opening, follow the selection and piercing instructions below. For a punch, select the complete punch model. Use a punch with straight sides, vertical walls and flat ends at the stock planes. Angled faces are supported. Leave at least 0.4 mm of stock around the nominal polygon. Acute corners can need more stock: the post also checks the intersection of the two offset face lines and the swept wire at that corner. CamCraft checks each corner with the rough offset for the selected stock thickness. The stock margin includes the 0.125 mm wire radius. Some reentrant contours are supported. A tight inside corner fails if the rough offset leaves more than 0.002 mm at the nominal vertex. Short segments and closely spaced faces fail if adjacent rough paths could meet. The punch must have a straight outer face that allows the lead to stay entirely on the waste side. The punch must have one boundary and no cavities, steps or other bodies. Select a 0.25 mm wire and condition **AGIE_QN2**. Set the work planes to the stock top and bottom, and specify how the punch is captured. The capture setting confirms support for the punch when it is released. Keep the wire vertical. Taper, four-axis, burnout, explicit skims, tabs and fixture models are unsupported.
+4. Place the centre of a predrilled 2 mm threading hole in the waste. The entire hole must be inside the stock. Allow a perpendicular approach to a straight face with at least 3 mm of lead and at least 3 mm of straight face on each side of the entry. Generate the operation.
 5. Open **Post**, choose **One program** and keep the general post settings at their defaults. Under **Agie technology**, set **Separation cut length (mm)** to **1.0**. Zero leaves the separation unspecified and blocks the post. This length applies to the separation segment that Agie Control generates. Check its position, trims and release sequence in the control’s job preview. Enter the parent folder and a fresh **Job folder name** such as `PUNCH40`. Use up to eight uppercase letters or digits, beginning with a letter. The post publishes the entire directory after validation. To retain an earlier job, give the new one a different name.
 
+### Select a die opening
+
+Use a 20 mm thick retained plate with one through-opening, planar caps and vertical walls. In the Wire Contour Geometry tab, choose **Edges** and Shift-click the connected edges of its upper opening rim. Set the wire side to **Die**. Set **Freed piece captured** when the setup can hold the released slug. Place the complete 2 mm threading hole inside the opening, with at least 3 mm between its centre and the entry face. Leave 3 mm of straight face on each side of the perpendicular entry. The supported opening is a convex polygon with corners that the rough wire can reach within 0.002 mm.
